# UPSTREAM SOURCE (not FreeLinX patches, not generated):
#   NetBSD 10.1 `/bin/sh` -- the Almquist shell (ash) used by NetBSD.
#   In the NetBSD source tree it lives at:
#       external/bsd/bin/sh
#   Full NetBSD base src set (contains bin/ and external/, including sh):
#       https://cdn.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-10.1/source/sets/src.tgz
#
# The NetBSD 10.1 release src set is immutable and reproducible. See
# https://www.netbsd.org/releases/formal-10/NetBSD-10.1.html and
# https://cdn.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-10.1/source/sets/SHA512 for the
# release checksums published by the NetBSD project.
#
# Relevant sh sources under that tree:
#   external/bsd/bin/sh/{main.c, eval.c, exec.c, expand.c, redir.c, parse.c,
#   var.c, builtins.c, cd.c, mknodes.c,...}
